# act (nektos/act) default flags for local CI iteration.
#
# Usage: invoke `act` (or via tools/act-cell) from repo root; act reads
# this file automatically. See AGENTS.md §3.6 "Local CI iteration with
# act" for the operator-facing workflow.

# Runner images — catthehacker's "act" variants include the toolchain
# preinstalled in stock GitHub-hosted runners (apt, sudo, node, etc.).
# `act-latest` mirrors ubuntu-latest; `act-22.04` mirrors ubuntu-22.04
# (ci.yml's matrix only references ubuntu-latest today but the second
# mapping future-proofs the pinned-runner cells).
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P ubuntu-22.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04
-P ubuntu-24.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Force linux/amd64 even on Apple Silicon. Most GitHub Actions
# (setup-nim-action, actions/cache@v4) only ship amd64 binaries; arm64
# emulation via Docker Desktop's qemu is slow (3-5x) but correct.
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Reuse containers across runs of the same job so dep installs cache.
# Combine with `--rm` on the CLI if you want a clean slate.
--reuse

# Pull images on first reference, then leave alone. Avoids re-pulling
# the ~2GB catthehacker image on every invocation.
--pull=false
